# RX Engine Verification Environment

This project implements a UVM-based verification environment for the RX Engine DUT.

The design under test is an encrypted RX Engine RTL module.  
The testbench contains an RX agent, virtual interface, sequence items, sequences, scoreboard, coverage collector, reference model, and top-level testbench.

## Directory Structure

```text
├── filelist_rx.f                    # Compile order management file
├── Makefile
├── README                           # This file
├── rtl/
│   └── rx_eng.vp                    # DUT: Encrypted RX Engine RTL code
└── testbench/
    ├── agent_rx/
    │   ├── rx_agent.sv              # rx_agent_c: instantiate sequencer, driver, input monitor and output monitor
    │   ├── rx_driver.sv             # rx_driver_c: drive transactions onto input interface
    │   ├── rx_in_monitor.sv         # rx_in_monitor_c: sample DUT inputs, publish request to scoreboard
    │   ├── rx_out_monitor.sv        # rx_out_monitor_c: sample DUT outputs, publish response to scoreboard
    │   ├── sequences/
    │   │   └── rx_sequence.sv       # rx_sequence_c: generate and manage transaction sequences
    │   └── transactions/
    │       ├── rx_payload_body.sv   # rx_payload_body_c: data payload top class
    │       ├── rx_req_trans.sv      # rx_req_trans_c: request transactions used by DUT input
    │       └── rx_rsp_trans.sv      # rx_rsp_trans_c: response transactions used by DUT output
    │
    ├── interfaces/
    │   └── rx_intf.sv               # Virtual interface for both DUT and TB
    │
    ├── packages/
    │   └── packet_base_trans.sv     # Base transaction for all transactions
    │
    ├── tb_env/
    │   ├── rx_coverage.sv           # rx_coverage_c: RX Engine coverage collector
    │   ├── rx_env.sv                # rx_env_c: wire agent, scoreboard and coverage
    │   ├── rx_ref_model.sv          # rx_ref_model_c: reference model for DUT function
    │   ├── rx_scoreboard.sv         # rx_scoreboard_c: check correctness of results
    │   └── uvmtb_rx.sv              # Top-level testbench
    │
    └── tests/
        └── rx_test.sv               # Launch sequence, report coverage and pass/fail
